 "notes": "Printed p.149 (concluded). Mother tongue Sindhi (cols 16-20; subsidiary Rajasthani, Gujarati), Panjabi (cols 21-25; subsidiary Rajasthani, Sindhi) and Gujarati (cols 26-32; subsidiary Bhili, Rajasthani, Sindhi). The row label spells it 'Paragna' here, against 'Pargana' on leaf 336. The Gujarati block is very faintly printed and the scan breaks up the digits. Two figures are unreadable ('?'); several others are read with moderate confidence: Marwar Rajasthani males 131, Sirohi Rajasthani females 830, SW Mewar Rajasthani 122/132. Gujarati speaker counts match Part I Gujarati persons for Marwar 613, Sirohi 3,196, Banswara 475 and Kushalgarh 410; they are tract figures for Jaisalmer 70 (the Part I state figure is also 70) and Mewar 354."
